10.text:
PUBLIC RESPONSE: The passage is usually quoted from Borges’ discussion of Argentine nationalism, El escritor argentino y la tradición / The Argentine Writer and Tradition, in the Inquisiciones / El tamaño de mi esperanza group of pieces, the text that is habitually rendered as “The National Character / El carácter nacional”.

There Borges illustrates “las ilusiones del patriotismo no tienen fin / the illusions of patriotism have no end” with the classic patriotic commonplaces:

* Greek – the Athenian statesman/orator Pericles, the Funeral Oration in Thucydides;
* Englishman – William Shakespeare, the patriotic apostrophe to England in Richard II, “This blessed plot, this earth, this realm, this England…”;
* German – Johann Wolfgang von Goethe, the canonical German national poet-philosopher whose Deutschland is constantly invoked in the 19th-c. German patriotic tradition.

Pericles, William Shakespeare, Johann Wolfgang von Goethe

