11.text:
The passage is the patriotic-illusion paragraph of *El escritor argentino y la tradición* – “The Argentine Writer and Tradition”, 1932, reprinted in *Discusión / Otras inquisiciones / Other Inquisitions*.

There Borges writes “las ilusiones del patriotismo no tienen fin / the illusions of patriotism have no end” and illustrates the topos with the three canonical national self-encomia:

* Greek – the Funeral Oration of Athens, the Periclean voice of Athenian superiority;
* English – the patriotic encomium as it is conventionally quoted by Borges as Samuel Johnson;
* German – the linguistic-nationalist encomium conventionally quoted by Borges as Johann Gottfried Herder.

Pericles, Samuel Johnson, Johann Gottfried Herder

